Proposals by Mr. Furber and ideas I had:
    [X] extend assembly language using syntax to differentiate between registers and immediates, like:
        "add r0 r1 #3           ; adds register 1 and number 3 together and writes back to register 0"

    [ ] implement basic parallelization

    [X] add support for inline immediates
    [X] add encapsulated operations, allowing you to calculate two things at once:
        "sub r2 (xor r0 #6) r1  ; subtracts register 1 from the result of bitwise-xoring register 0 with 0b110"

Things I added on top of this (QoL/comfort features):
    [X] add preprocessor directives to improve assembly readability
